@* InboxPage: the work waiting for the signed-in user, at "/inbox". The inbox is also the notification list: every row
   is computed from the review data when the page opens, so there is nothing to clear except the "New" markers.

   Four groups, in this order: "To sign" (a reviewer slot of the user without a current signature), "Replies waiting"
   (someone answered in a thread of the user, or on the user's own review), "Failed checks" (the user's own review has
   checks answered Fail) and "Updates" (a review of the user was approved, rejected or reopened by someone else since the user
   last looked; for information only and not counted as work). A review can appear in several groups. Each row links
   to the review, shows why it is listed as a chip, a "New" marker when the reason happened after the user last saw
   the review, and the due date (marked when overdue) for the groups that need action. "Mark all as read" marks
   every listed review as seen.

   Presentation only; state lives in InboxPage.razor.cs. Every interactive element and every key value carries a
   stable kebab-case data-testid (row-level ids carry the 1-based position of the row), and the data-interactive
   marker on the root flips to "true" once the live circuit is connected.

   Human factors: (a) the summary line says in one sentence how much needs action; (b) the empty state tells the user
   plainly that nothing is waiting instead of showing a blank page; (c) the reason is a short chip, never color
   alone; (d) the whole row is one link to the review.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/inbox"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Inbox - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page" data-testid="inbox-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <div class="page-heading">
        <h1>Inbox</h1>
        @if (Items.Count > 0)
        {
            <button type="button" data-testid="inbox-mark-read" @onclick="MarkAllReadAsync">Mark all as read</button>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="page-lead" data-testid="inbox-summary">@Summary</p>

    @if (ActionCount == 0)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="inbox-empty">Nothing needs your action.</p>
    }

    @foreach (var section in Sections)
    {
        var rows = Items.Where(item => item.Section == section).ToList();
        if (rows.Count == 0)
        {
            continue;
        }

        <h2 class="section-title" data-testid="inbox-section-@SectionKey(section)">@SectionTitle(section)</h2>
        <ul class="row-list" data-testid="inbox-list-@SectionKey(section)">
            @foreach (var item in rows)
            {
                var n = Items.IndexOf(item) + 1;
                <li class="row-card" data-testid="inbox-row-@n">
                    <div class="row-main">
                        <a class="row-title" href="/projects/@item.ProjectId/reviews/@item.ReviewId" data-testid="inbox-link-@n">@item.Title</a>
                        <p class="muted" data-testid="inbox-review-@n">@item.ProjectName / @item.ReviewId</p>
                        @if (item.Detail is { } detail)
                        {
                            <p class="muted" data-testid="inbox-detail-@n">@detail</p>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-meta">
                        @if (item.IsUnread)
                        {
                            <span class="badge unread" data-testid="inbox-unread-@n">New</span>
                        }
                        <span class="badge @ChipClass(item)" data-testid="inbox-chip-@n">@item.Chip</span>
                        @if (item.DueDate is { } due)
                        {
                            <span class="badge @(item.IsOverdue ? "failed" : null)" data-testid="inbox-due-@n">@(item.IsOverdue ? "Overdue" : "Due") @due.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
